LineComment   "// Accessors and static functions: a getter computes a property read"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// (value.name), a setter computes the next value a property write rebinds"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// (local.name = v), and a static fn is a function scoped to its type, called"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// Type.name(...) — the Type.Name path enum members and associated constants"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// already take. A getter and a setter are pure by construction: there is no"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// syntax to give an accessor an effect, so a field-spelled read can never hide"
Newline       "\n"
LineComment   "// IO behind it — the guarantee an AI-facing language wants from `value.name`."
Newline       "\n"
